  }
}
```

Tamsin closes the ledger on her thumb, then slides the thumb free. She counts your offer against the sweating pipes overhead, and it seems to come out in your favor.

<npc>"A fair cut, from a woman who anchored without being asked. I'll take it,"</npc> she says. <npc>"Here's your first payment: someone has been selling the lanes' timings by the hour. A man called Juro, always adorned in bright thread. He drinks at the water-board end of the docks."</npc>

She lowers her voice. <npc>"He's trying to leave a rival behind. Ask him how."</npc>

