Tamsin doesn't look up. "Tide's a generous word on a dock with no sea," she says. "Come back and the manifest is dry. Don't, and it stays dry anyway." Behind you, Juro's footsteps retreat, unhurried, toward the water-board end. He stops there and turns his untouched cup a quarter-turn on the counter, watching your back the whole way.

*Binding that promise to a vow of its own would be a Swear an Iron Vow.*

